# 8b, 8d and 8n: a worker asks and blocks. One question the lead agent
# answers itself; the other it hands to the person, who answers it in the
# action pane with a button, takes that back inside its four seconds, and
# answers again. Each worker goes on with exactly the answer that stood.
agent A.1: ask "tabs or spaces?" | expect-answer spaces | write-result | report done "spaces it is"
agent B.1: ask "which colour?" --options red,blue | expect-answer blue | write-result | report done "blue it is"

file brief.md: Target: a page | Change: your part | Constraints: none | Ownership: your file | Acceptance: the check
orch: init
orch: run new "two questions"
task A "Indent the file" --name indenting --check "exit 0" --brief brief.md
task B "Paint the wall" --name painting --check "exit 0" --brief brief.md
orch: start A
await: attempts A.1 asked
orch: start B
await: attempts B.1 asked
orch: wait --timeout 10                             -> expect question q1 q2
orch: status                                        -> expect asking 'answer q1 "<answer>"' "escalate q1"
orch: answer q1 spaces
await: attempts A.1 reported
orch: escalate q2                                   -> expect "for the person"
orch: answer q2 red                                 -> expect exit 5 "--relayed"

pane actions: 100x20
expect-row "which colour?"
click "[ Red ]"
expect-row "u to undo"
await: q2 state answered answer red
key u
await: q2 state open
click "[ Blue ]"
await: q2 state answered answer blue; attempts B.1 asked
clock +5s
await: attempts B.1 reported; q2 state used
orch: wait --ack last --timeout 10                  -> expect answered blue done
assert: no event lost; no event twice
